-- The passage questions as drills (drill-engine plan §3 step 6): each question that has an answer
-- gets its options, written from that answer — the right one(s) and wrong ones a careful reader
-- could take for it. Kept in options_json beside the question:
--
--   { "ask_en":      the question as the drill asks it,
--     "interaction": "choose" | "choose_all",
--     "options":     [...],  in no particular order (the drill shuffles them)
--     "correct":     [indices into options],
--     "explain_en":  what rises after the answer (a source may be named here, never asked) }
--
-- How they are written:
--   · they test the text — its words, its language, an accurate picture of what it says: an
--     accurate rendering, what a word or root pictures, what a construction does to the meaning.
--     No structure trivia, no hypotheticals. Where the slide's question was of that kind, ask_en
--     asks something concrete of the same āyah instead.
--   · Arabic is written in Arabic, never transliterated (Rule 1).
--   · never who said it (Rule 0): a question about a scholar or a book is asked of the text.
--
-- Questions with no answer to mark (reflection prompts, "open answer") keep options_json NULL:
-- they stay discussion cards for the Table, outside the drill engine. 12:1-7 has no answers
-- written yet, so none of its questions is drillable. The 39 questions stay draft (unreviewed);
-- only live questions are drawn.

-- ── Ghāfir 40:1–3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Render v.2 accurately: تَنزِيلُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْعَلِيمِ","interaction":"choose","options":["The sending down of the Book is from Allah, the Mighty, the Knowing","Allah sent down the Book on a blessed night, the Mighty, the Knowing","The Book descends upon the Mighty, the Knowing","The Book was sent down from Allah, the Mighty, the Wise"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"تَنزِيلُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ is the subject, مِنَ ٱللَّهِ its predicate: the sending down of the Book is from Allah. The two names are ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْعَلِيمِ — not ٱلْحَكِيمِ, which opens سورة الزمر. حمٓ stands on its own before it."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:01';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Who is the Book said to come from, and by which two names?","interaction":"choose","options":["From Allah, ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْعَلِيمِ: the Mighty, the Knowing","From Allah, ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَكِيمِ: the Mighty, the Wise","From Allah, ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ: the Merciful, the Compassionate","From the Lord of the worlds, ٱلسَّمِيعِ ٱلْبَصِيرِ: the Hearing, the Seeing"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"From Allah, ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْعَلِيمِ. سورة الزمر opens with ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَكِيمِ; here ٱلْعَلِيمِ says God knows where to place His message."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:02';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Why تَنزِيل and not إِنزَال? What does the doubled form add?","interaction":"choose","options":["Sending down in stages, over time","Sending down all at once","Sending down with great force","Sending down to many prophets"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"تَنزِيل is the verbal noun of نَزَّلَ (form II): sending down in instalments. The objectors complained the Qurʾān was not sent down all at once (25:32); the sūra’s first word asserts exactly that."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:03';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Which of the four names of v.3 draw the listener in, rather than hold him back?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["غَافِرِ ٱلذَّنۢبِ — Forgiver of sin","قَابِلِ ٱلتَّوْبِ — Accepter of repentance","شَدِيدِ ٱلْعِقَابِ — Severe in punishment","ذِى ٱلطَّوْلِ — Owner of bounty"],"correct":[0,1,3],"explain_en":"Three draw in (ٱلتَّرْغِيب); شَدِيدِ ٱلْعِقَابِ alone holds back (ٱلتَّرْهِيب) — the whole pressing toward what the sending down is for."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:04';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Render شَدِيدِ ٱلْعِقَابِ accurately","interaction":"choose","options":["Severe in punishment","Swift in reckoning","Mighty in power","Painful in torment"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"شَدِيد is severe, hard; ٱلْعِقَاب is the punishment that follows a deed, at its heel (the root ع ق ب). Swift in reckoning is سَرِيعُ ٱلْحِسَابِ; painful torment is عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:05';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Why is it hard to read شَدِيدِ ٱلْعِقَابِ as a plain description of ٱللَّه, like the names around it?","interaction":"choose","options":["شَدِيد is an adjective joined to its own subject (شَدِيدٌ عِقَابُهُ), which does not make it definite — yet it would describe the most definite name there is","Because شَدِيد is a verb, not a noun","Because it is plural and ٱللَّه is singular","Because it alone stands in a different case from the names around it"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"A صِفَة مُشَبَّهَة joined to its own subject never becomes definite by that joining, so it should not describe a definite name. It is read as a description all the same (the names of God are lasting, so it is definite after all), or as a substitute (بَدَل)."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:06';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Why can’t غَافِرِ ٱلذَّنۢبِ and قَابِلِ ٱلتَّوْبِ mean the same thing?","interaction":"choose","options":["Two names joined side by side would be empty repetition if they meant the same, so each adds its own meaning","Because one speaks of this world and the other of the next","Because one is for the prophets and the other for everyone","They do mean the same: the second only repeats for rhythm"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"Two names joined by وَ cannot mean the same thing. If غَافِرِ ٱلذَّنۢبِ meant forgiving after repentance it would repeat قَابِلِ ٱلتَّوْبِ, so it reaches further: forgiving the sin itself."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:07';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"In لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ, what is the predicate of لَا?","interaction":"choose","options":["It is left unsaid and understood: مَوْجُود (‘existing’)","إِلَٰهَ","هُوَ","إِلَّا"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"لَا denies the whole kind; إِلَٰهَ is its noun, built on fatḥa; the predicate is left unsaid (مَوْجُود). إِلَّا is the particle of exception and هُوَ stands in for the hidden pronoun. No god exists — but He."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:08';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"In إِلَيْهِ ٱلْمَصِيرُ, what does putting إِلَيْهِ first do?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["It restricts: to Him, and to no other","It keeps the verse ending in the sūra’s rhyme","It turns the phrase into a question","It places the return in this world"],"correct":[0,1],"explain_en":"إِلَيْهِ is the predicate brought forward, ٱلْمَصِيرُ the subject held back. To Him alone is the return; and the verse ends, like its neighbours, on a long vowel then a consonant."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:09';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"ٱلْعِقَاب (v.3) shares its root ع ق ب with عَاقِبَة (‘how it ended’, v.21). What does the root picture?","interaction":"choose","options":["What comes after, at the heel: the outcome that follows a deed","A sudden blow that comes from nowhere","A long delay before anything happens","A chain that binds the hands"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"عَقِب is the heel; ع ق ب is what follows on behind. ٱلْعِقَاب is the punishment that follows the deed, and عَاقِبَة is how a thing ends up — ‘travel the land and see how it ended for those before them’ (v.21) points back to شَدِيدِ ٱلْعِقَابِ."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:10';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Verse 2 makes its claim with no إِنَّ and no لَ of emphasis, though its hearers deny it. Why?","interaction":"choose","options":["The denier is spoken to as one who does not deny: the proofs around him leave him no ground for denial","Because its hearers already believed it","Because the claim was uncertain","Because emphasis is never used at the opening of a sūra"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"تَنْزِيلُ ٱلْمُنْكِرِ مَنْزِلَةَ غَيْرِ ٱلْمُنْكِرِ: the evidence around the denier is such that he had no business denying at all, so he is spoken to plainly."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:40:1:11';

-- QR:Q:40:1:12 is a reflection with an open answer: no options, it stays a Table card.

-- ── al-Dukhān 44:1–9 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"وَٱلْكِتَٰبِ ٱلْمُبِينِ (v.2): what does God swear by?","interaction":"choose","options":["The Clear Book itself — the very thing disputed is what is sworn by","The blessed night of v.3","The heavens and the earth","The life of the Prophet"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"وَ is the وَاو of the oath; ٱلْكِتَٰبِ ٱلْمُبِينِ is the Book that makes things plain. Swearing by the contested revelation makes it its own proof."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:1:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Which of these hold for لَيْلَةٍ مُّبَٰرَكَةٍ (v.3)?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["In the language: a night of abundant, lasting good","It is the night named in 97:1, لَيْلَةِ ٱلْقَدْرِ, in the month of 2:185","It is certainly the middle night of شَعْبَان","The word مُّبَٰرَكَة itself gives the night’s date"],"correct":[0,1],"explain_en":"مُبَارَكَة, from ب ر ك: abundant good that stays. By 97:1 and 2:185 the night is لَيْلَةُ ٱلْقَدْرِ in رَمَضَان; the mid-شَعْبَان view is weak. Keep the word’s meaning and the night’s identity apart."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:3:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"فِيهَا يُفْرَقُ كُلُّ أَمْرٍ حَكِيمٍ (v.4): what does يُفْرَقُ picture?","interaction":"choose","options":["Each wise matter is set apart and made distinct — the year’s affairs apportioned, while the eternal decree does not change","The eternal decree is rewritten every year","Matters are mixed together and left undecided","Only the verses of the Qurʾān are divided up"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"يُفْرَقُ, passive of فَرَقَ: to part one thing from another, make it distinct. On that night each wise matter of the year is set out and apportioned — a ledger for the year, not a change in the eternal decree."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:4:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"أَمْرًا مِّنْ عِندِنَآ (v.5): which readings of أَمْرًا does the Arabic allow?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["A state (حَال): sent down as a command from Us","A purpose (مَفْعُول لَهُ): sent down for the sake of a command from Us","The subject of the sentence","A call: ‘O command’"],"correct":[0,1],"explain_en":"As حَال it says how it was sent down; as مَفْعُول لَهُ it says why. The parse changes the English: ‘as a command’ or ‘for a command’."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:5:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"رَحْمَةً مِّن رَّبِّكَ (v.6): why ‘your Lord’ rather than ‘from Us’?","interaction":"choose","options":["It ties the mercy to His lordship over you: being your Lord entails mercy","To show the mercy comes through an angel","Because ‘from Us’ would be ungrammatical here","To turn to a different audience"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"Naming رَبِّكَ where a pronoun would do binds mercy to lordship: ٱلرُّبُوبِيَّة entails ٱلرَّحْمَة. Then إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ: هُوَ restricts — He alone is the Hearing, the Knowing."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:6:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"رَبِّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ (v.7) is read رَبِّ and رَبُّ. What does each reading do?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["رَبِّ: it continues رَبِّكَ of v.6, as a substitute (بَدَل)","رَبُّ: it starts a new statement — ‘He is the Lord…’","رَبِّ: it becomes a call, ‘O Lord’","رَبُّ: it becomes the object of ‘sends down’"],"correct":[0,1],"explain_en":"With kasra, رَبِّ follows رَبِّكَ as a بَدَل: ‘mercy from your Lord — Lord of the heavens…’. With ḍamma it is cut off as a new sentence: ‘He is the Lord of the heavens…’."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:7:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"v.8: لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ يُحْىِۦ وَيُمِيتُ — what does the second half add to the first?","interaction":"choose","options":["Its proof: He gives life and gives death, so He alone is God","A new subject: the Day of Judgement","A condition: only if He wills","A contrast: others also give life"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ denies every god but Him; يُحْىِۦ وَيُمِيتُ is the proof — power over life and death belongs to the only God."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:8:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Render v.9 accurately: بَلْ هُمْ فِى شَكٍّ يَلْعَبُونَ","interaction":"choose","options":["Yet they are in doubt, playing about","Indeed they are certain, and in earnest","But they doubted, then believed","Rather, they were playing before the doubt came"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"بَلْ turns away from what came before: after certainty sworn in 1–8, yet they are in doubt. يَلْعَبُونَ is a present state beside it — playing, not taking it seriously."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:44:9:1';

-- ── al-Zumar 39 (draft: written, not yet reviewed) ───────────────────────────

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Which two names open the sūra (v.1), and why do they suit a call to sincere worship?","interaction":"choose","options":["ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَكِيمِ: His command can be enforced, and it is rightly placed","ٱلْغَفُورِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ: so every sin can be forgiven","ٱلسَّمِيعِ ٱلْعَلِيمِ: He hears every prayer","ٱلْأَوَّلِ ٱلْآخِرِ: He outlasts all"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"ٱلْعَزِيز and ٱلْحَكِيم: might guarantees the command can be enforced, wisdom that it is rightly placed — together grounding the claim to worship Him alone."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:1:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"أَمَّنْ هُوَ قَٰنِتٌ ءَانَآءَ ٱلَّيْلِ (v.9): who is being described?","interaction":"choose","options":["One devoutly obedient through the hours of the night, who also knows","One who knows, even without worship","One who worships out of habit","One who gives away the most wealth"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"قَانِت: devoutly obedient, standing long in prayer; ءَانَآءَ ٱلَّيْلِ: the hours of the night. The verse goes on: are those who know and those who do not alike?"}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:1:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ (v.10): what is promised to the patient?","interaction":"choose","options":["Their reward without measure: uncounted","A reward exactly equal to their deeds","A reward in this world only","Forgiveness, but no reward"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ: without counting. The reward of ٱلصَّبْر is not weighed and measured as other deeds are."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:2:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"Which images does the passage use for the two destinies?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["ظُلَلٌ مِّنَ ٱلنَّارِ: canopies of Fire above them and below (v.16)","غُرَفٌ مِّن فَوْقِهَا غُرَفٌ: chambers built above chambers, rivers flowing beneath (v.20)","A bridge stretched over a valley","A garden as wide as the heavens and the earth"],"correct":[0,1],"explain_en":"ظُلَل, layered canopies of Fire (v.16), against غُرَف built one above another, with rivers flowing beneath (v.20)."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:2:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"أَفَمَن شَرَحَ ٱللَّهُ صَدْرَهُۥ لِلْإِسْلَٰمِ (v.22): what sets this breast apart from the hardened heart?","interaction":"choose","options":["It is upon light from its Lord, while the other is hardened against the remembrance of God","It knows more of the law","It is spared every hardship","It belongs to a prophet only"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"شَرَحَ: opened wide. فَهُوَ عَلَىٰ نُورٍ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ — and woe to those whose hearts are hardened (ٱلْقَٰسِيَةِ) against the remembrance of God."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:3:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"The parable of v.29: رَجُلًا فِيهِ شُرَكَآءُ مُتَشَٰكِسُونَ and رَجُلًا سَلَمًا لِّرَجُلٍ. What does it picture?","interaction":"choose","options":["A slave owned by quarrelling partners lives in conflict; one owned wholly by one master is at peace — so serve One","That slaves should be freed","That two masters give twice the care","That service to anyone is the same"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"مُتَشَٰكِسُونَ: partners at odds, pulling against each other; سَلَمًا: wholly and peaceably one man’s. Divided service is conflict; worship is owed to One."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:3:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"فَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ (v.32): who is the most unjust?","interaction":"choose","options":["One who lies against God and denies the truth when it comes to him","One who wrongs his neighbour","One who forgets a prayer","One who doubts but keeps searching"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"مِمَّن كَذَبَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ وَكَذَّبَ بِٱلصِّدْقِ إِذْ جَآءَهُۥ: who lied against God and called the truth a lie when it came to him."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:4:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"أَلَيْسَ ٱللَّهُ بِكَافٍ عَبْدَهُۥ (v.36): what does the question do?","interaction":"choose","options":["It affirms: yes, He suffices — so there is no need for other protectors","It is a real question, left open","It complains against God","It denies that God helps"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"A question that asks for a yes (ٱسْتِفْهَام تَقْرِيرِيّ): God is enough for His servant, so the gods they threaten him with are nothing."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:4:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"ٱللَّهُ يَتَوَفَّى ٱلْأَنفُسَ حِينَ مَوْتِهَا وَٱلَّتِى لَمْ تَمُتْ فِى مَنَامِهَا (v.42): what does يَتَوَفَّى picture?","interaction":"choose","options":["Taking the soul back in full — at death, and in sleep, some kept and some sent back for a set term","The soul leaving God’s hold in sleep","Rest for the body only","Dreams that show the future"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"تَوَفَّى: to take something in full. He takes souls at death and in sleep, keeps the one decreed to die and sends the other back إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:5:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"قُل لِّلَّهِ ٱلشَّفَٰعَةُ جَمِيعًا (v.44): to whom does intercession belong?","interaction":"choose","options":["To God, all of it","To the angels","To the righteous dead","To the idols, by God’s leave"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"لِّلَّهِ … جَمِيعًا: all intercession is His — refuting the intercessors the idolaters relied on."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:5:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ ٱلذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا (v.53) is followed by وَأَنِيبُوٓا۟ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكُمْ (v.54). What does the promise carry with it?","interaction":"choose","options":["Turning back to Him and submitting before the punishment comes","That nothing at all is asked of the sinner","That only small sins are forgiven","That forgiveness comes only after punishment"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"أَنِيبُوا: turn back, again and again. The promise is to those who turn back and submit before the punishment comes."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:6:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"How do vv.53–55 hold together?","interaction":"choose_all","options":["لَا تَقْنَطُوا۟ مِن رَّحْمَةِ ٱللَّهِ: v.53 forbids despair and opens forgiveness of every sin","vv.54–55 command turning back and submitting before the punishment comes suddenly","vv.54–55 cancel the promise of v.53","v.53 was for the Prophet’s companions only"],"correct":[0,1],"explain_en":"لَا تَقْنَطُوا: do not despair. The promise stands, and the next two verses tell how to meet it: turn back and submit before the punishment comes بَغْتَةً, suddenly."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:6:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"أَفَغَيْرَ ٱللَّهِ تَأْمُرُوٓنِّىٓ أَعْبُدُ أَيُّهَا ٱلْجَٰهِلُونَ (v.64): what does the address ٱلْجَٰهِلُونَ say of the demand?","interaction":"choose","options":["That it comes from ignorance of God","That it is a matter of taste","That it is acceptable under pressure","That it is a sign of wisdom"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"ٱلْجَٰهِلُونَ: you who do not know. Asking him to worship other than God is called what it is: ignorance."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:7:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"How does v.67 picture God’s majesty?","interaction":"choose","options":["وَٱلْأَرْضُ جَمِيعًا قَبْضَتُهُۥ … وَٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتُ مَطْوِيَّٰتٌۢ بِيَمِينِهِۦ: the whole earth in His grasp, the heavens folded in His right hand","A throne set over the water","Light upon light","The sky raised without pillars"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"قَبْضَة: a handful, a grasp; مَطْوِيَّات: rolled up, folded — on the Day of Resurrection."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:7:2';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"زُمَرًا (vv.71, 73): what does the word picture?","interaction":"choose","options":["Throngs, company after company: the deniers driven to Hell, the God-fearing led to the Garden","The trumpet that is blown","The scrolls laid open","The angels around the Throne"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"زُمَر, plural of زُمْرَة: a throng, a group moving together. Both companies go in crowds — and the sūra is named for them."}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:8:1';

UPDATE qr_study_question SET options_json = '{"ask_en":"How do the greetings at the two gates differ (vv.71–73)?","interaction":"choose","options":["Hell’s keepers rebuke — أَلَمْ يَأْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنكُمْ; the Garden’s greet — سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ طِبْتُمْ فَٱدْخُلُوهَا","Both sets of keepers greet with peace","Neither gate has keepers","Hell’s keepers are silent"],"correct":[0],"explain_en":"‘Did messengers from among you not come to you?’ against ‘Peace be upon you, you have done well, so enter.’"}', updated_at = datetime('now') WHERE id = 'QR:Q:39:8:2';

